{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"patriotic-valued-hog","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nADR 0056 already extracted `interpret_failure`, settings/usage builders, Agent kwargs, success logging, spend recording, and the provider session guard. ADR 0058 later removed per-file headroom assertions and made the locked 800-LOC module limit the only LOC ceiling. Current `origin/main` nevertheless has a 785-line `runner.py` and a 388-line `PydanticAIRunner.run()`.\n\nThis second pass must identify an ownership improvement in today's call graph. It must not repeat prior extraction, duplicate `ProviderSession` or `ExitStack`, introduce a generic hook/plugin bus, revive rejected frozen carriers without new evidence, or add a function-size ratchet.\n\n## Work\n\n- Map the exact effect/resource timeline: event-loop displacement; config/preflight; tracing; provider/session construction; model/fallback scope; capability/cache/web settings; Agent execution; failure accounting; answer attribution; pre-finalization logging; finalization; run-shape/spend recording.\n- Inventory semantic references plus string imports, monkeypatch targets, compatibility re-exports, globals mutated by alias, and tests that inspect source.\n- Build a fault matrix for every raising boundary and identify the current owner of cleanup, accounting, provenance, and error translation.\n- Compare candidate seams against `providers`, `model_classes`, `structured_run`, `agent_call`, `runner_support`, and ADRs 0056/0058. Prefer strengthening an existing owner.\n- Record the ADR disposition before implementation. If the structure changes an accepted decision, complete the full ADR lifecycle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The research record names every effect/resource boundary, its owner, its required ordering, and the observed behavior when it raises.\n- [ ] Semantic and text/string consumer censuses agree or every discrepancy is explained; monkeypatch and compatibility hazards are assigned to the change that moves/removes them.\n- [ ] A red-capable fault matrix covers raises before/after provider creation, fallback entry, external execution, finalization, and telemetry/accounting.\n- [ ] The selected design states exactly which existing module/class/function gains responsibility and which code is deleted; it does not create a second session owner or generic lifecycle framework.\n- [ ] Mutable provenance/settings and post-call answer attribution are modeled honestly; no decorative frozen carrier is proposed.\n- [ ] No function-NLOC ratchet, per-file headroom assertion, or new hard size threshold is proposed. Size measurements may be reported as advisory debt signals only.\n- [ ] The research critique identifies unanswered assumptions and conflicts; any necessary ADR amendment is explicitly approved/merged before implementation, or the record explains why ADR 0056 already authorizes the seam.","id":"c465-b475-acc8-48a6","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["architecture","llm","research"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Revalidate PydanticAIRunner lifecycle ownership against current architecture"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788026450689385502,"uuid":"d9602fb3-ebff-4808-a917-4840ee03de53"}